WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:03.067
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:05.334
Welcome. Please. Yes.
You're the guest.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.567
-There you go.
-You're the guest.

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:09.067
-I'm so used to waiting
for the other person.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.400
-Yeah, this is --
I'm interviewing you.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.667
-I'm loving it.
-You know --

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:12.767
-I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:14.133
-I'm so happy you're here.
-Can I say that?

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:18.133
I have wanted to be on
this television show since I --

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.300
since the second you started
hosting it.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.734
I don't know if I would have
ever hosted my show

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:25.467
if it wasn't for watching
you do this show

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:26.868
and all the people you have
here.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:29.601
And as we sat here now,
I am thrilled to be

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:30.634
on "The Tonight Show."

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:31.801
I mean it from the bottom
of my heart.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:33.434
-I love you man.
-I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:34.934
-You know, at first --
-I really am.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.634
-When I first met you,
before you were hosting

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:37.934
the show,
I knew you as an actor.

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:39.467
-Mm.
-You're a phenomenal actor,

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:42.634
and, everyone, watch "Mammals"
on Prime Video.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:44.567
Watch just the first episode
if you haven't seen it.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:46.167
If you don't like it,
you don't have to watch the --

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.667
You'll be sucked into it.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:50.167
Even the last three seconds,
I'm like, oh, my God.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:53.267
-It twists and turns
all over the place.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:55.267
-You are fantastic, buddy.
-You are so kind. Thank you.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.801
-It's your first time here
on our show,

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:59.234
but we've hung out many a time.
-We have.

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:01.067
-We have many fun adventures
together.

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.334
-Well, it's always fun.

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:03.767
-[ Laughs ]
-It's never not fun.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:05.667
That's the beauty of it.
If I go to something --

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:09.133
because often, obviously, Jimmy
and I will be invited to things,

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:12.567
And you get there, and I always
feel like I shouldn't be there.

00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:14.067
Someone's going to tap me
on the shoulder and go,

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:16.234
"There's been a huge mistake."

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:17.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:20.934
-You should leave.
-Yeah. James Cameron we met.

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:22.834
-Not James.
-Then, when I see you, I think,

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.300
"Oh, okay, this is going
to be fun."

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.968
And we have this -- and I can't
remember who started it,

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:29.434
whether I started it or you
started it, this running bit

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:33.133
that we have where we see
each other at an event --

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:35.000
Because also, have you noticed,
we go to things

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.734
and no one ever sits us
together.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:37.868
We're on different tables.

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:39.567
It's like they got to spread
the talkers.

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:40.734
-[ Laughs ]
-Do you know what I mean?

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.400
-They know we're trouble
when we get together.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.067
-So we started --
I think it was me who started

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:47.667
because I came over
to your table, and you had --

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:50.100
I think it was a tequila,
a glass of tequila,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.234
and you were just about to grab
it to take a drink,

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:55.267
and I swooped in, picked it up,
looked you dead in the eye,

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.734
and drunk the whole thing.
-Drunk the whole thing.

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:58.334
-And put it back.
-Yeah. Exactly, yeah.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:04.501
-And this then set in motion
a constant running joke where --

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:07.400
-Any time we saw each other,
I go like, "Can I have a sip

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.767
of what -- can I have a sip?"
-Oh, sure.

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:10.234
You got a bad voice? Yeah, yeah.
There you go. Yeah.

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:12.067
-And then I just chug the whole
drink until it's empty,

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.334
then give it back to you.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:15.100
-The entire thing.
And it always makes me laugh.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:18.000
-Do you remember you were
sitting next to Lady Gaga once?

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.267
-Do I remember?
Of course I remember.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:24.000
It was insane. We're at this --
I'm sat next to Lady Gaga.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.033
Right? I'm here.
She's there.

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:28.434
And she's lovely.
She's amazing.

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:29.667
And we're talking.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:33.801
And she was saying to me
that she's very nervous

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:34.968
about her performance.

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:36.100
She was going to perform
that night,

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.634
and she said
she was very, very nervous.

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:39.067
And I was like,
"But you're Lady Gaga.

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:40.467
You don't get nervous."

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:44.234
And she said, "No, I'm more
comfortable in a big stadium

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.834
than I am in front
of a small room like this."

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.000
And I said, "You're going to be
great."

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.400
And she said,
"Will you pray with me?"

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.234
-Yes.
-Right? And I went, sure, yeah.

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:56.567
Let's --

00:02:56.567 --> 00:03:01.033
And she held my hand like this,
and she closed her eyes,

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:02.234
and we're literally like this.

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:03.901
She closed her eyes,
and she started saying,

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:05.868
"Please give me the strength
to perform."

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:08.667
And I opened my eyes slightly,
and in the corner of my eye,

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:12.667
I can see Jimmy walking towards
my drink to do the bit.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:13.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:15.367
And I'm going like this,
I'm going like this --

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:17.667
I'm going like this.
I'm going -- I'm going --

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:20.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:26.601
And I'm going like this, "Hmm,
yes, give us the strength."

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:28.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.467
And he goes -- he goes to me --

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:31.868
He goes later -- You came over.

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:34.334
-Because I did a good job.
-He looked and was like, okay.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:35.767
And he came back.
He went, "What was going on?"

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:39.367
I said, "We, We --
We were just praying."

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:40.701
-What are you guys doing?
You were praying.

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.267
-We were praying.
-And then I drank your drink.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.801
-And then you drank our drinks.

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:45.901
You announced you're leaving
"The Late Late Show"

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.934
this coming spring.
-Yes.

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:49.334
-Very sad. I know. We love you.

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:52.100
Do you have anything planned
for the end?

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.033
-I've actually just been asked
to take over "The Tonight Show,"

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.567
which is really weird.

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:58.501
-Hey, that's a mistake!
Wait! No!

00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:01.033
No! I can't -- Please, no!

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:02.601
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:05.968
No, my biggest plan -- well,
my intention,

00:04:05.968 --> 00:04:09.467
which I think I'll fail
at dramatically,

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:14.567
is to just not be just, like,
crying for the entire hour,

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.300
which I think I will be.
-Yeah.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.667
-So I'm really going to try
and keep it together.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:21.167
Our intention is to, you know,
go out in the way

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:24.701
that we came in,
and I will miss it hugely.

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:26.100
I will miss it every day.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.901
I will miss the people
that I work with.

00:04:27.901 --> 00:04:30.834
And there's no sense of me
leaving because I don't love it.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:34.100
I'm just leaving the show
primarily because

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:39.067
we're a long way from home,
and we really want our children

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:41.267
to know what it's like
to grow up in London,

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:44.601
to have a solid relationship
with their grandparents,

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:47.367
and that is time that you don't
get back, really.

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:50.634
So, however hard it is to go,
I'm completely certain

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:52.467
that it's the right thing
to do it.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:55.868
And, you know, I've loved every
second of doing it.

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:57.701
I love it. I love the show.
I really do.

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:59.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:02.334
-Let's talk about "Mammals."
-Yeah.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:03.701
-Can I say that? Can I --
-Yeah, sure. Go for it.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.033
-Can I give a little spoiler?

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:06.934
-Yeah, it's always impossible
not to spoil the show

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:07.934
if you're going to talk
about it, but you can.

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:10.167
-It's a dark comedy.
-Yes.

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:13.534
-With some very dramatic scenes,
very funny scenes.

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:15.801
I think that only you
could pull this off.

00:05:15.801 --> 00:05:17.300
You do such a great job of this.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.501
Who wrote this, by the way?

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:20.534
-The show is written by
an incredible writer

00:05:20.534 --> 00:05:23.467
called Jez Butterworth,
who has written --

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:25.000
He's got the most extraordinary
career.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.234
He's basically written
two Tony award-winning plays,

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:30.667
but he's also written
two "Bond" movies,

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:34.033
the new "Indiana Jones,"
and "Ford versus Ferrari."

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.567
-Wow.
-So he's got this kind of

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:38.834
incredible -- and what he's done
in the show is make something

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:43.467
very small about love
and relationships and marriage

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:46.501
with all of the kind of twists
and turns that you would get

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:48.868
in one of his kind
of bigger movies.

00:05:48.868 --> 00:05:50.234
I'm incredibly proud of it.

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:52.534
-It starts off with
you guys traveling.

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:54.367
You're going to
this beautiful place in England.

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:56.234
-In Cornwall. The coast, yeah.
-Cornwall?

00:05:56.234 --> 00:05:59.400
-Beautiful, and your wife is
pregnant, and she's beautiful,

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.767
and you guys are just
the perfect couple,

00:06:00.767 --> 00:06:02.067
and the sunset,
and it's all great.

00:06:02.067 --> 00:06:05.934
-Yes.
-And then she loses the baby.

00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:08.901
-So they lose their baby and
it's really sad.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.200
It's awful.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.367
And he's got her phone
because there's bad service

00:06:12.367 --> 00:06:14.934
where they are in Cornwall,
and he looks down at his phone

00:06:14.934 --> 00:06:18.934
and he realizes in that moment
that she's having an affair.

00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:23.000
And in that moment,
he also bumps into the singer,

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.400
Tom Jones.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.167
-[ Laughs ] Yeah. So --
So he's trying not to freak out

00:06:27.167 --> 00:06:30.000
that Tom Jones is there, but
then your life is falling apart.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.767
-Correct.

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:33.667
-And it gets trickier
after that.

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:35.868
It just gets trickier
upon trickier upon trickier.

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:37.634
It's so great
and so worth it.

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:38.901
I want to show a clip.

00:06:38.901 --> 00:06:41.033
Here is James Corden
and Tom Jones in "Mammals."

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.300
Take a look.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.467
-You're my neighbor, right?

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:46.434
I'm Tom from next door.
Pleased to meet you.

00:06:47.701 --> 00:06:50.434
I don't know about you,
but I'm coming back.

00:06:50.434 --> 00:06:52.934
I mean, this is like a landscape
you already know.

00:06:52.934 --> 00:06:56.400
It's like something that's --
that's etched in your soul.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.834
Do you ever get that?

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:00.934
-[ Vomiting ]

00:07:00.934 --> 00:07:02.901
-Are you all right?
-[ Coughing ]

00:07:02.901 --> 00:07:06.567
-What?

00:07:06.567 --> 00:07:08.334
[ Vomiting ]

00:07:08.334 --> 00:07:10.000
Jesus Christ.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.968
What was it, an oyster
or something?

00:07:11.968 --> 00:07:14.367
-[ Sniffs ]

00:07:18.234 --> 00:07:20.200
Tom Jones.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.701
-Yeah.

00:07:23.234 --> 00:07:26.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.234
-Tom Jones.

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:31.234
I want to say thank you so much
for coming on,

00:07:31.234 --> 00:07:36.367
but I love doing late night
with you in the same school

00:07:36.367 --> 00:07:37.968
and us doing the show together.

00:07:37.968 --> 00:07:40.701
I'm going to miss that
and seeing your bits.

00:07:40.701 --> 00:07:42.467
You would do things that would
make me want

00:07:42.467 --> 00:07:43.701
to be better at my job.

00:07:43.701 --> 00:07:45.033
So, I want to thank you
for everything you do.

00:07:45.033 --> 00:07:46.501
-You're welcome.
I love you.

00:07:46.501 --> 00:07:48.734
I love you so much.
I really do.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:49.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:49.901 --> 00:07:51.067
-James Corden, everyone.

00:07:51.067 --> 00:07:53.834
"Mammals" is streaming now
on Prime Video.

00:07:53.834 --> 00:07:55.734
Jenna Ortega joins us
after the break.

00:07:55.734 --> 00:07:56.968
Stick around, everybody.

